## Array Algorithms

### Finding Minimum and Maximum

```java
public static int findMin(int[] arr) {
    int min = arr[0];
    for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (arr[i] < min) {
            min = arr[i];
        }
    }
    return min;
}
```

Start with the first element, then compare against all others. Using `Integer.MAX_VALUE` as the initial value also works.

### Computing Averages

```java
public static double average(int[] arr) {
    int sum = 0;
    for (int val : arr) {
        sum += val;
    }
    return (double) sum / arr.length;
}
```

Note the cast to `double` to avoid integer division.

### Shifting Elements

**Left shift** (removing element at index `pos`):
```java
for (int i = pos; i < arr.length - 1; i++) {
    arr[i] = arr[i + 1];
}
// Last element is now a duplicate; set to default or reduce logical size
```

**Right shift** (inserting at index `pos`):
```java
for (int i = arr.length - 1; i > pos; i--) {
    arr[i] = arr[i - 1];
}
arr[pos] = newValue;
```

### Reversing an Array

```java
public static void reverse(int[] arr) {
    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length / 2; i++) {
        int temp = arr[i];
        arr[i] = arr[arr.length - 1 - i];
        arr[arr.length - 1 - i] = temp;
    }
}
```

Swap elements from the outside in. Stop at the middle.

### Linear Search

```java
public static int linearSearch(int[] arr, int target) {
    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (arr[i] == target) {
            return i;
        }
    }
    return -1;   // not found
}
```

### Removing Duplicates (Logical)

```java
// Count unique elements
public static int countUnique(int[] sorted) {
    if (sorted.length == 0) return 0;
    int unique = 1;
    for (int i = 1; i < sorted.length; i++) {
        if (sorted[i] != sorted[i - 1]) {
            unique++;
        }
    }
    return unique;
}
```

### Checking for Duplicates

```java
public static boolean hasDuplicates(int[] arr) {
    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        for (int j = i + 1; j < arr.length; j++) {
            if (arr[i] == arr[j]) {
                return true;
            }
        }
    }
    return false;
}
```

### String Array of Digits

```java
// Extract digits of a number into an array
public static int[] getDigits(int n) {
    String s = Integer.toString(Math.abs(n));
    int[] digits = new int[s.length()];
    for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
        digits[i] = s.charAt(i) - '0';
    }
    return digits;
}
```

### Common Mistakes

**Mistake 1: Integer division in average.** `sum / arr.length` truncates. Cast to double first.

**Mistake 2: Shifting in the wrong direction.** When left-shifting, go left to right. When right-shifting, go right to left. Otherwise you overwrite values before copying them.

**Mistake 3: Not handling empty arrays.** Check `arr.length == 0` before accessing `arr[0]`.

