## Recursive Search & Sort

### Recursive Binary Search

Binary search naturally maps to recursion -- each step halves the search space:

```java
public static int binarySearch(int[] arr, int target, int low, int high) {
    if (low > high) {
        return -1;            // base case: not found
    }

    int mid = (low + high) / 2;

    if (arr[mid] == target) {
        return mid;            // base case: found
    } else if (arr[mid] < target) {
        return binarySearch(arr, target, mid + 1, high);  // search right half
    } else {
        return binarySearch(arr, target, low, mid - 1);   // search left half
    }
}

// Initial call:
int index = binarySearch(arr, target, 0, arr.length - 1);
```

### Merge Sort

Merge sort is the classic recursive sorting algorithm:

**Divide:** Split the array in half.
**Conquer:** Recursively sort each half.
**Combine:** Merge the two sorted halves.

```java
public static void mergeSort(int[] arr, int left, int right) {
    if (left >= right) return;    // base case: 0 or 1 elements

    int mid = (left + right) / 2;
    mergeSort(arr, left, mid);       // sort left half
    mergeSort(arr, mid + 1, right);  // sort right half
    merge(arr, left, mid, right);    // merge the halves
}

private static void merge(int[] arr, int left, int mid, int right) {
    int[] temp = new int[right - left + 1];
    int i = left, j = mid + 1, k = 0;

    while (i <= mid && j <= right) {
        if (arr[i] <= arr[j]) {
            temp[k++] = arr[i++];
        } else {
            temp[k++] = arr[j++];
        }
    }
    while (i <= mid) temp[k++] = arr[i++];
    while (j <= right) temp[k++] = arr[j++];

    for (k = 0; k < temp.length; k++) {
        arr[left + k] = temp[k];
    }
}
```

### Merge Sort Trace

```
[38, 27, 43, 3, 9, 82, 10]
Split: [38, 27, 43] and [3, 9, 82, 10]
Split: [38] [27, 43] and [3, 9] [82, 10]
Split down to single elements...
Merge: [27, 38] [3, 43] [3, 9] [10, 82]
Merge: [3, 27, 38, 43] [3, 9, 10, 82]
Merge: [3, 3, 9, 10, 27, 38, 43, 82]
```

### Recursive String Processing

```java
// Count occurrences of a character
public static int countChar(String s, char c) {
    if (s.length() == 0) return 0;
    int count = (s.charAt(0) == c) ? 1 : 0;
    return count + countChar(s.substring(1), c);
}

// Remove all occurrences of a character
public static String removeChar(String s, char c) {
    if (s.length() == 0) return "";
    String rest = removeChar(s.substring(1), c);
    if (s.charAt(0) == c) return rest;
    return s.charAt(0) + rest;
}
```

